{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541362-beast-lair-chambers","id":541362,"title":"Beast: Lair Chambers","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-05T09:51:30-07:00","id":541362,"title":"Beast: Lair Chambers","content":"1. How large can a Chamber be? And how small can it be?<br /> <br /> 2. Can you have wildlife in a Chamber? Like say poisonous serpents or spiders?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6154-deathmonkee","name":"DeathMonkee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T10:17:04-07:00","id":541414,"title":"","content":"1) As large or small as you want (though you and others still need to be able to get through it) it runs on dream logic so navigating the a Chamber the size of the Sahara would be surprisingly easy without the &quot;Maze&quot; trait. <br /> <br /> 2) As long as the wildlife can't directly effect those within, yes. if it can effect those within it needs to be represented by a Trait (Stinging, Swarms and even Jagged could do the trick)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T10:47:40-07:00","id":541446,"title":"","content":"Hmmmmmm................but if I'm reading this right, each chamber has to be at least based off of a &quot;real&quot; place, either in reality or in another plane of existence.<br /> <br /> 3. Would it be possible to have a Locus in one of your Chambers? The book talks about how you need to defend yourself, having a few large spirits making a home in your Chambers sounds like a good defense to me, and not one most would think of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6154,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6154-deathmonkee","user":"DeathMonkee","date":".  Explained my thought process better. 06-05-2015, 01:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6154-deathmonkee","name":"DeathMonkee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T13:15:46-07:00","id":541628,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't allow the Locus in the Chamber. I suppose you could base a Chamber on a location where one is, then when you enter the Primordial Pathway there'd likely be a Spirit or two coming in to the Chamber as it manifests, though that's risky business. Spirits are pretty Blue and Orange morality and can as easily attempt to bring down your Chamber and Lair as attack any other intruders that happen to be about in it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T13:19:13-07:00","id":541631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541362-beast-lair-chambers?p=541628#post541628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't allow the Locus in the Chamber. I suppose you could base a Chamber on a location where one is, then when you enter the Primordial Pathway there'd likely be a Spirit or two coming in to the Chamber as it manifests, though that's risky business. Spirits are pretty Blue and Orange morality and can as easily attempt to bring down your Chamber and Lair as attack any other intruders that happen to be about in it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Presumably, such a Locus would be in a Lair that has conditions that Resonate with the Spirits coming through, making a spirit unlikely to want to destroy that part of the lair,<br /> <br /> Since Geist Kinship can put an Avernian Gate in your Lair, I don't see why you couldn't have a Locus, since an Avernian Gate is arguably like a Locus to the Underworld.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T13:37:32-07:00","id":541644,"title":"","content":"I need to read more on the Kinship... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I'm finding it hard to track where all that is though, the document having 'refer to p.XX' isn't very helpful... ^_^;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T14:32:35-07:00","id":541692,"title":"","content":"I'm reading up on Primordial Pathways, and you can enter the Shadow using them, so arguably some sort of connection already exists. I don't see why you couldn't have a Locus there as well for either a few large spirits or a horde of small spirits to feed on. There are already merits for having spirits as either friends or allies/pets/slaves, so it is possible/probable/somewhat-likely to happen.<br /> <br /> And whenever you are feeling especially generous you could drag a particularly evil human into one of your Chambers to be punished(if you are a Nemesis).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6154-deathmonkee","name":"DeathMonkee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T02:55:04-07:00","id":542406,"title":"","content":"Yeah, you can access the Anima Mundi through the Pathways, which is essentially the dreamworld of Spirits.<br /> <br /> Though I still can't see anywhere in Kinship where you can get an Avernian Gate though. The Beasts can use Skeleton Key to make an Avernian Gate open to the Primordial Dream, though I think that's different from them actually owning something like that as a permanent fixture in their Chamber.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T04:54:38-07:00","id":542446,"title":"","content":"I don't think you can put a locus or avernian gate <i>in</i> your lair. Mostly because they are defined as a path between the shadow/underworld and the material. A path between the shadow and the primordial dream is called a primordial pathway. <br /> <br /> You could theoretically give a spirit free access to your lair, but they'd need to open it at a resonant location just like everyone else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T05:37:19-07:00","id":542473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DeathMonkee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541362-beast-lair-chambers?p=541446#post541446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmmmmm................but if I'm reading this right, each chamber has to be at least based off of a &quot;real&quot; place, either in reality or in another plane of existence.<br /> <br /> 3. Would it be possible to have a Locus in one of your Chambers? The book talks about how you need to defend yourself, having a few large spirits making a home in your Chambers sounds like a good defense to me, and not one most would think of.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I think any dangers within your lair are represented as traits regardless. Like Gnomish said. The threats aren't there in the physical sense, they're just nightmares, reflections of a possible threat that people fear.<br /> <br /> <br /> If you don't have any traits, the snakes just sort of slither around menacingly. But if you get stinging and / or venomous, they might lash out and bite at intruders. If the snakes are constrictor species, the lair might have Crushing, in which they try to ensnare and squeeze their victims.<br /> <br /> <br /> I would imagine a chamber based on the inside of a snake's digestive track to have Cramped, Slick and Corrosive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 06-06-2015, 08:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T08:36:03-07:00","id":542640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541362-beast-lair-chambers?p=542406#post542406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though I still can't see anywhere in Kinship where you can get an Avernian Gate though. The Beasts can use Skeleton Key to make an Avernian Gate open to the Primordial Dream, though I think that's different from them actually owning something like that as a permanent fixture in their Chamber.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541362-beast-lair-chambers?p=542446#post542446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think you can put a locus or avernian gate <i>in</i> your lair.</div> </div> </div> </div>Chapter Five.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>p313</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Forming a Kinship bond with a spirit or an Uratha sometimes creates a portal within the Beast\u2019s Lair that opens into the Shadow, though this is rare and usually happens only with spirits of high Rank or werewolves of high Primal Urge and low Harmony.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>p318</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">When one of the Bound forms a Kinship bond with a Child of the Dark Mother, her little corner of the Beast\u2019s Lair takes on an aspect of death reflecting her geist. [\u2026] The presence of one of the Bound brings a new concept into the Lair, one that interacts strangely with astral space. Sometimes it creates an Avernian Gate, a doorway to the Underworld direct from the Dream.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T08:48:56-07:00","id":542646,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ITS POSSIBLE!!!!!!<br /> I just squealed in happiness, thank you!<br /> <br /> So, that begs the question: Are spirits by default manifest in the primordial dream?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6154-deathmonkee","name":"DeathMonkee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T09:04:04-07:00","id":542653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541362-beast-lair-chambers?p=542640#post542640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Chapter Five.<br /> <i>Originally posted by <b>p313</b></i><br /> <i>Forming a Kinship bond with a spirit or an Uratha sometimes creates a portal within the Beast\u2019s Lair that opens into the Shadow, though this is rare and usually happens only with spirits of high Rank or werewolves of high Primal Urge and low Harmony.</i><br /> </div> </div> </div> </div>That's not a locus. That would probably be something Astral Realms calls a &quot;Shadow Gate&quot;. A locus has some sort of material focus and produces essence. This would lack those features.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T10:22:17-07:00","id":542735,"title":"","content":"Shadowgates are cWoD..........were they re-published?<br /> <br /> And loci CAN have a material focus to be mobile, or they can be focused on a place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6154,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6154-deathmonkee","user":"DeathMonkee","date":". 06-06-2015, 01:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6154-deathmonkee","name":"DeathMonkee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T21:53:25-07:00","id":543467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DeathMonkee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541362-beast-lair-chambers?p=542646#post542646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ITS POSSIBLE!!!!!!<br /> I just squealed in happiness, thank you!<br /> <br /> So, that begs the question: Are spirits by default manifest in the primordial dream?</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought as much, though I would need to double check <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/50992/Astral-Realms?cPath=1_267\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Astral Realms</i></a> to be sure. I haven't heard anything about that changing in 2nd ed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T07:45:21-07:00","id":543891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DeathMonkee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541362-beast-lair-chambers?p=542646#post542646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ITS POSSIBLE!!!!!!<br /> I just squealed in happiness, thank you!<br /> <br /> So, that begs the question: Are spirits by default manifest in the primordial dream?</div> </div> </div> </div> I presume you mean capable of physical interaction, I believe so yes. <br /> <br /> It wouldn't actually be manifested as 2 ed uses the term, because that's dependent on conditions which I don't think would relevent. <br /> <br /> While different types of ephemeral beings can't normally interact in twilight, that was never a problem for ephemeral beings who are actually in an otherworld. So a ghost in an astral realm can interact with everything as if it were the underworld, etc, I don't remember the issue being addressed in second edition but I doubt it will change.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T11:14:05-07:00","id":544047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541362-beast-lair-chambers?p=543891#post543891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I presume you mean capable of physical interaction, I believe so yes.<br /> <br /> It wouldn't actually be manifested as 2 ed uses the term, because that's dependent on conditions which I don't think would relevent.<br /> <br /> While different types of ephemeral beings can't normally interact in twilight, that was never a problem for ephemeral beings who are actually in an otherworld. So a ghost in an astral realm can interact with everything as if it were the underworld, etc, I don't remember the issue being addressed in second edition but I doubt it will change.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that was what I was thinking. Anyone else have any questions about Lairs? I think all of mine have been answered by this and the other thread.<br /> <br /> Thank you all for the assistance and the conversation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6154-deathmonkee","name":"DeathMonkee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T11:25:02-07:00","id":544064,"title":"","content":"Brood lairs: Can you enter/exit from any chamber automatically, or do you need to exchange Be My Guest invites first?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T11:55:01-07:00","id":544109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541362-beast-lair-chambers?p=544064#post544064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Brood lairs: Can you enter/exit from any chamber automatically, or do you need to exchange Be My Guest invites first?</div> </div> </div> </div>See page 123: &quot;A Beast whose Lair is part of a Brood Lair (that is, shares at least one Chamber with another Beast or has a Burrow crossing between their Lairs) may include one Trait from any other Beast in the brood when imposing Traits, either as the existing Trait used for resonance or one of those imposed.&quot;<br /> <br /> Between that and the ease of opening Primordial Pathways to other Lairs it's relatively simple to get to elsewhere in a broodmate's Lair even without adding another Burrow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T11:57:12-07:00","id":544113,"title":"","content":"Sorry, I can see how my phrasing may have been ambiguous now. <br /> <br /> Can you use another broodmate's chamber to exit <i>the lair itself</i>? Like, to the material.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T23:15:26-07:00","id":544848,"title":"","content":"Yes. A beast can use Primordial Pathways to move from a Chamber to any location resonant to that Chamber. You can go to any world you want; hedge, underworld, shadow, material, etc. You can go to a random location resonant with the Chamber to any world you want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T23:53:33-07:00","id":544861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541362-beast-lair-chambers?p=544064#post544064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Brood lairs: Can you enter/exit from any chamber automatically, or do you need to exchange Be My Guest invites first?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Since the Lair is an extension of their soul and they're sharing it, I would imagine they can cross over freely between each Chamber. Besides, it says bringing somebody into a brood Lair threatens the whole brood, not just you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}